BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain TCP Congestion Control, detailing the roles of the Congestion Window \(cwnd\), Slow Start Threshold \(ssthresh\), and Slow Start phase.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Congestion control throttles traffic to protect intermediate network routers from packet drop) Tj
T*
(   collapse. The sender maintains a Congestion Window \(cwnd\) alongside rwnd, sending at most) Tj
T*
(   min\(rwnd, cwnd\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Congestion Window \(cwnd\): A dynamically adjusted upper limit on the number of unacknowledged) Tj
T*
(   bytes the sender may inject into the network based on perceived network capacity.) Tj
T*
(   2. Slow Start Threshold \(ssthresh\): A variable that determines whether TCP operates in) Tj
T*
(   exponential Slow Start or linear Congestion Avoidance.) Tj
T*
(   3. Slow Start Phase:) Tj
T*
(   - At connection start or after RTO timeout, cwnd initializes to 1 to 10 MSS.) Tj
T*
(   - For each segment acknowledged, cwnd increases by 1 MSS. Since every segment in the window) Tj
T*
(   generates an ACK, cwnd doubles every Round-Trip Time \(RTT\), producing exponential growth \(1 ->) Tj
T*
(   2 -> 4 -> 8 -> 16 MSS\).) Tj
T*
(   - Slow start continues until cwnd reaches ssthresh, whereupon TCP switches to Congestion) Tj
T*
(   Avoidance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 12:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Congestion Avoidance, Fast Retransmit, and Fast Recovery phases in TCP Reno.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   TCP Reno enhances basic congestion control by mitigating the severe performance penalties of) Tj
T*
(   timeout resets:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Congestion Avoidance: Once cwnd >= ssthresh, exponential growth stops. Instead, cwnd) Tj
T*
(   increases additively by approximately 1 MSS per RTT \(specifically, cwnd = cwnd + MSS * \(MSS /) Tj
T*
(   cwnd\) for each ACK received\). This linear growth cautiously probes for available bandwidth.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Fast Retransmit: When a single segment is lost, subsequent out-of-order segments cause the) Tj
T*
(   receiver to return identical duplicate ACKs. Upon receiving three duplicate ACKs \(4 identical) Tj
T*
(   ACKs total\), the sender infers packet loss immediately, retransmitting the missing segment) Tj
T*
(   before the RTO timer expires.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Fast Recovery: Instead of dropping cwnd to 1 MSS \(as in Tahoe\), Reno halves ssthresh) Tj
T*
(   \(ssthresh = cwnd / 2\), sets cwnd = ssthresh + 3 MSS, and inflates cwnd for additional duplicate) Tj
T*
(   ACKs. Once the missing segment is acknowledged, cwnd resets to ssthresh and resumes linear) Tj
T*
(   congestion avoidance.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 13:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
