(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   TCP relies on four core timers to maintain protocol integrity across asynchronous networks:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Retransmission Timer \(RTO\): Set whenever a segment is sent. If unacknowledged when RTO) Tj
T*
(   expires, the segment is retransmitted, RTO doubles \(exponential backoff\), and cwnd drops to 1) Tj
T*
(   MSS.) Tj
T*
(   2. Persistence Timer: Solves zero-window deadlock. When the receiver advertises rwnd = 0, the) Tj
T*
(   sender starts the persistence timer. Upon expiry, the sender transmits a 1-byte Window Probe to) Tj
T*
(   prompt an updated window advertisement.) Tj
T*
(   3. Keepalive Timer: Prevents resources from being tied up by orphaned idle connections \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   if a client powers off without teardown\). After 2 hours of inactivity, the server transmits) Tj
T*
(   probe packets. If no response after several probes, the server resets the session.) Tj
T*
(   4. TIME_WAIT Timer \(2MSL\): Maintains active-close socket resources for twice the maximum) Tj
T*
(   segment lifetime to ensure old packets dissipate and final ACKs arrive.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 19:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the Stream Control Transmission Protocol \(SCTP\) and compare its features with TCP and UDP.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   SCTP \(RFC 4960\) is a message-oriented, reliable transport protocol combining the best) Tj
T*
(   capabilities of TCP and UDP while introducing enterprise resilience features:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Message Framing: Unlike TCP's byte stream, SCTP preserves explicit application message) Tj
T*
(   boundaries \(like UDP\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Multi-Streaming: A single SCTP association supports multiple independent logical streams. A) Tj
T*
(   dropped packet in stream 1 blocks only stream 1, eliminating head-of-line blocking for other) Tj
T*
(   streams.) Tj
T*
(   3. Multi-Homing: An SCTP association binds multiple IP addresses per endpoint \(e.g., dual) Tj
T*
(   Ethernet NICs\). Traffic automatically fails over to backup IP paths without terminating the) Tj
T*
(   session.) Tj
T*
(   4. Security: SCTP replaces the 3-way handshake with a 4-way handshake using signed) Tj
T*
(   cryptographic cookies, providing native immunity against SYN flood attacks.) Tj
T*
(   5. Primary Use: Telephony signaling \(SS7 over IP / SIGTRAN\), multimedia streaming, and) Tj
T*
(   carrier-grade infrastructure.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 20:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain QUIC protocol architecture, highlighting why it is built on UDP and how it solves TCP head-of-line blocking.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   QUIC \(RFC 9000\) is a modern transport protocol engineered by Google and standardized by IETF to) Tj
T*
(   replace the legacy TCP+TLS+HTTP/2 stack in HTTP/3:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Why QUIC is Built Over UDP:) Tj
T*
(   Modifying OS kernels and enterprise firewalls to support a new Layer 4 protocol requires) Tj
T*
(   decades \('protocol ossification'\). By encapsulating in standard UDP datagrams, QUIC runs) Tj
T*
(   entirely in user-space, enabling rapid browser updates and instant firewall compatibility.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Elimination of Head-of-Line Blocking:) Tj
T*
(   In TCP, HTTP/2 multiplexes multiple web streams over a single byte-stream connection. If a) Tj
T*
(   single packet drops, the entire TCP stream stalls while waiting for retransmission. QUIC embeds) Tj
T*
(   independent stream numbering inside UDP: if a packet belonging to stream 3 drops, streams 1, 2,) Tj
T*
(   and 4 continue processing without delay.) Tj
T*
ET

