(   state:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Legitimate Triggers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Non-Listening Port: If a SYN arrives at a destination IP and port where no listening socket) Tj
T*
(   process is registered, the OS returns RST+ACK.) Tj
T*
(   2. Half-Open / Orphaned Connections: If Host A crashes and reboots, any incoming segment from) Tj
T*
(   an existing session on Host B triggers an RST from Host A because the state was lost.) Tj
T*
(   3. Hard Abort: An application calling close\(\) with SO_LINGER set to timeout=0 discards) Tj
T*
(   remaining buffer bytes and sends RST to instantly terminate the session.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Malicious Triggers \(TCP Reset Attack\):) Tj
T*
(   An eavesdropping attacker who sniffs sequence numbers can forge an RST segment matching the) Tj
T*
(   active 4-tuple and in-window sequence number, causing routers or endpoints to tear down) Tj
T*
(   legitimate sessions \(used in state censorship and session hijacking\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
