(>> Solution to Question 24:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain TCP Maximum Segment Size \(MSS\) negotiation and how Path MTU Discovery avoids transport-level fragmentation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   MSS Negotiation:) Tj
T*
(   1. MSS represents the maximum application data payload a TCP entity is willing to accept in a) Tj
T*
(   single segment.) Tj
T*
(   2. During the SYN handshake, each host announces its local MSS based on its outgoing interface) Tj
T*
(   MTU: MSS = MTU - 40 \(20 bytes IPv4 header + 20 bytes TCP header\). For standard 1500-byte) Tj
T*
(   Ethernet, MSS = 1460 bytes. The effective MSS for the connection is min\(Client_MSS,) Tj
T*
(   Server_MSS\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Path MTU Discovery \(PMTUD\):) Tj
T*
(   If an intermediate tunnel link has a smaller MTU \(e.g., 1400 bytes\), segments of 1460 bytes) Tj
T*
(   would require IP fragmentation. To prevent this, TCP sets the Don't Fragment \(DF\) bit in all IP) Tj
T*
(   datagrams. If an intermediate router cannot forward without fragmenting, it drops the datagram) Tj
T*
(   and returns ICMP Type 3 Code 4 \('Fragmentation Needed and DF set'\), including the link's MTU.) Tj
T*
(   TCP then scales down its MSS accordingly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss TCP Half-Close, detailing socket programming semantics and realistic use cases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   A TCP connection is composed of two independent unidirectional byte streams. TCP Half-Close) Tj
T*
(   occurs when one endpoint finishes sending data but wishes to continue receiving data from the) Tj
T*
(   remote peer:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Socket API Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Calling standard close\(sockfd\) tears down both read and write channels.) Tj
T*
(   - Calling shutdown\(sockfd, SHUT_WR\) performs a half-close: it transmits a FIN segment to the) Tj
T*
(   remote peer, closing the outbound send stream, while leaving the inbound receive buffer open.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Realistic Use Case \(Remote Command Execution / Sorting Server\):) Tj
T*
(   A client uploads a large 50 MB unsorted dataset to a remote computing service. When upload) Tj
T*
(   finishes, the client executes shutdown\(SHUT_WR\). The server sees EOF, processes the entire) Tj
T*
(   dataset, and streams back the sorted result. The client reads the result completely and issues) Tj
T*
(   the final close.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
