(>> Solution to Question 29:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain TCP Fast Open \(TFO, RFC 7413\) and its impact on web page loading performance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Standard TCP requires a full Round-Trip Time \(RTT\) handshake before application data \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   HTTP GET\) can be transmitted. TCP Fast Open eliminates this startup latency for repeat visits:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Operation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Initial Session: The client requests a TFO Cookie by sending a standard SYN with an empty) Tj
T*
(   TFO option. The server returns a cryptographic cookie in its SYN+ACK.) Tj
T*
(   2. Subsequent Sessions: When connecting to the same server, the client sends a SYN containing) Tj
T*
(   the cached TFO Cookie AND the initial application request \(HTTP GET\) inside the SYN payload.) Tj
T*
(   3. Immediate Execution: The server validates the cookie and hands the application request to) Tj
T*
(   the web server daemon immediately, returning HTTP response data inside the SYN+ACK.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Performance Impact: Saves an entire RTT \(typically 50-150 ms\) on every subsequent TCP) Tj
T*
(   connection, substantially accelerating mobile browsing and high-latency web transactions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the mathematical stability of the Additive Increase Multiplicative Decrease \(AIMD\) algorithm using Chiu-Jain vector diagrams.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Chiu and Jain proved that among linear control policies, AIMD is the only mechanism that) Tj
T*
(   guarantees convergence to both Efficiency and Fairness in a shared bottleneck link:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Vector Diagram Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   Consider two TCP users \(x1 and x2\) sharing a bottleneck link of capacity C:) Tj
T*
(   1. Efficiency Line: Defined by x1 + x2 = C. Operating below this line underutilizes bandwidth;) Tj
T*
(   operating above causes packet loss.) Tj
T*
(   2. Fairness Line: Defined by x1 = x2 \(a 45-degree ray through the origin\). Points on this ray) Tj
T*
(   represent equal bandwidth sharing.) Tj
T*
(   3. Additive Increase Vector: Both users increment window by 1 MSS: \(x1 + 1, x2 + 1\). On the 2D) Tj
T*
(   Cartesian plane, this vector moves at a 45-degree angle parallel to the fairness line,) Tj
T*
(   improving efficiency.) Tj
T*
(   4. Multiplicative Decrease Vector: Upon congestion, both halve windows: \(x1 / 2, x2 / 2\). This) Tj
T*
(   vector points directly toward the origin along a ray connecting the current state to \(0,0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Convergence: The combination of parallel shift during increase and radial pull toward the) Tj
T*
(   origin during decrease forces any arbitrary initial state \(x1, x2\) into an oscillating limit) Tj
T*
(   cycle converging directly onto the intersection of the Fairness line and Efficiency line.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
